      "answer": "In Gloomhaven (2nd Edition), *advantage* works with attack modifier cards as follows:\n\n> With **advantage**, the attacker draws two modifiers and uses one of them. A monster always uses the better one, but a character may use either one.\n\n**Special handling for rolling modifiers:** If the first draw is a rolling modifier, you keep drawing modifiers one at a time until you get a non-rolling one, then draw one final modifier (ignoring any rolling icon on it). With *advantage*, you use all the initial rolling modifiers plus whichever of the last two modifiers you choose.\n\n**Key additional rules:**\n- An attack cannot gain multiple instances of *advantage* or *disadvantage*. If an attack has both, it is considered to have neither.\n- If the first draw is not a rolling modifier but the second is, the rolling icon on the second modifier is still ignored.",
